 "signs": [
  {
   "x": 29,
   "y": 14,
   "text": "CARDIFF CASTLE. Roman fort, then Norman keep, then Victorian fantasy. The Marquess of Bute spent a fortune on towers."
  },
  {
   "x": 53,
   "y": 12,
   "text": "BUTE PARK. 56 hectares, the River Taff, and a lot of cricket. Please do not feed the gulls. They have learnt to ask."
  },
  {
   "x": 22,
   "y": 31,
   "text": "CARDIFF ARENA. Home of rugby, concerts and the roof that rains inside. Entry through the big door. Dry feet not guaranteed."
  },
  {
   "x": 35,
   "y": 22,
   "text": "WALES MILLENNIUM CENTRE. The poem on the front reads, in Welsh: 'Creu gwir fel gwydr o ffwrnais awen'. Creating truth like glass from the furnace of inspiration."
  },
  {
   "x": 29,
   "y": 32,
   "text": "CARDIFF BAY. Once the biggest coal port in the world. Now, the biggest puddle with a view."
  },
  {
   "x": 23,
   "y": 33,
   "text": "PIERHEAD BUILDING. 1897, red terracotta. The Senedd is next door. They're very polite to each other."
  },
  {
   "x": 50,
   "y": 32,
   "text": "NORWEGIAN CHURCH. Roald Dahl was christened here. He didn't write about the font, but he did write about the giants."
  }
 ],
